                            {
                                "target_word": "racialized",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                        "entry_id": "fef669a1-5f45-3a41-8c9b-46d136e92167",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Connected to race or a specific race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6608c664-ff74-4d38-99fd-b9d78b9383f4",
                                                "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                                "text": "Writing on African Americans, Abdul Jan Mohamed suggests that \"Whereas bourgeois sexuality is a product of an empiricist, analytic, and proliferating discursivity, racialized sexuality is the product of a stereotypic, symbolizing , and condensing discursivity; the former is driven by a will to knowledge, the latter by both a will to conceal its mechanisms and its own will to power\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "858cbede-97ab-4c2a-abac-579fb351cbfd",
                                                "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                                "text": "Yet even seemingly secular colonial notions such as that of “a civilizing mission\" —or its more racialized version, “the white man's burden\" — or the 19th-century U.S. conviction of a \"manifest destiny\" have deep religious roots."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae463b67-8ce8-4921-a959-66209025e781",
                                                "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                                "text": "His [Oscar from Shark Tale] blackness is found not only in his accent and place of residence, but also in his mannerisms, behavior, and jewelry (that is, \"bling\"), which are highly racialized signifiers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5137c4e5-6ff4-4a4b-b2f1-a45021615945",
                                                "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                                "text": "Meaney demonstrates that in Australia, too, a prior emphasis on settler rights and constitutional principles gave way to a more racialized conception of Britishness from roughly mid-century."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75c0e32a-56eb-4d2e-a277-b8a627925e26",
                                                "sense_id": "a45e3584-35a6-3c39-93ab-e66e1ee29d55",
                                                "text": "That murkiness is important: some racialized ideas about suicide become so successfully naturalized that their origins seem to come from everywhere and nowhere. Today, some foundational assumptions live on intact (for example, the idea that native people \"preferred\" suicide), […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df0c1bbb-179c-3de2-b382-c0d1bccc201c",
                                        "entry_id": "fef669a1-5f45-3a41-8c9b-46d136e92167",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Influenced or determined by race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a483a1a4-e3fc-4aaf-9bbd-e2821032bcbf",
                                                "sense_id": "df0c1bbb-179c-3de2-b382-c0d1bccc201c",
                                                "text": "Thus somatic Feeling is not only racialized, but individualized, and moreover diversified in every individual, and according to successive Periods of Life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "439c93c2-c2e2-4898-9d5c-fc7729709e8c",
                                                "sense_id": "df0c1bbb-179c-3de2-b382-c0d1bccc201c",
                                                "text": "[…] tone and content of the discourse of manifest destiny shifted during the first half of the nineteenth century, becoming more racialized as the century progressed, as whites, especially white men, imagined themselves increasingly besieged by the sexualized presence and political aggressiveness of non-\"anglo-Saxon\" peoples, among them African Americans and \"waves\" of eastern and southern European immigrants (Haynes 1998)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "975c5537-318b-4da1-aefd-2143495087dd",
                                                "sense_id": "df0c1bbb-179c-3de2-b382-c0d1bccc201c",
                                                "text": "In the conclusion of his book, this insistence on redeeming the Volkstümlichkeit definitely took on more violent, more apocalyptic, and more racialized forms, which certainly call to mind early formulations of dubious “Blut und Boden\" ideologies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "617b98dc-b0b3-407b-9dfc-bdfa02eb770a",
                                                "sense_id": "df0c1bbb-179c-3de2-b382-c0d1bccc201c",
                                                "text": "At older ages, the system became more racialized, as the proportion of free black children serving under indenture was generally two to four times or more that of whites."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                        "entry_id": "fef669a1-5f45-3a41-8c9b-46d136e92167",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Divided and segregated along the boundaries of race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "434c1cdd-a61c-417b-b937-bda3caa3ba86",
                                                "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                                "text": "In a culture that was becoming increasingly more racialized, as music and entertainment industries were insisting on racial difference, Europe had to be true to the “spirit of a race” while creating a type of music that could appeal to a refined and \"proper\" white audience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "096ce8da-920d-421f-990d-bb3c3ea9e0d6",
                                                "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                                "text": "Though he consistently avoided systematic taxonomy of the human populations of Oceania, Prichard's division into classes became steadily more racialized."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6145108-e44e-42d1-9292-19b3183dffae",
                                                "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                                "text": "South Africa is not more racialized than China; Sweden is not less racialized than the United States."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f2c7b29-aefa-408c-a76a-83e01227ea64",
                                                "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                                "text": "That crystallized into a hard-and-fast creed, or into a sect within a creed, religion may easily become racialized, he [Rhys Davids] was fully ready to admit. But he believed that, as an instinct deep-rooted in the human heart, religion transcended the barriers of race, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95d22077-107a-4898-ae34-b4a73ce66c21",
                                                "sense_id": "1b85f29d-6606-3244-94a0-b827e92644d1",
                                                "text": "Or maybe public opinion became more racialized because the economic downturn pitted social groups against one another for scarce resources."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65c65e4f-9a9f-3abe-a810-d08d06d41be5",
                                        "entry_id": "fef669a1-5f45-3a41-8c9b-46d136e92167",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Othered; of color; considered as having a race, as contrasted with white people when considered as not having a race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a6b2bbc-39cc-4bb6-9c36-bdf91c312580",
                                                "sense_id": "65c65e4f-9a9f-3abe-a810-d08d06d41be5",
                                                "text": "This means that by disallowing legitimate claims to recognize and address issues of racism that impact the daily lives of Blacks and other racialized groups, an important and essential aspect of Black humanity and existence was also banished"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67a3f74d-bd51-4185-8a74-e060d0009b87",
                                                "sense_id": "65c65e4f-9a9f-3abe-a810-d08d06d41be5",
                                                "text": "In the 1980s racialized activists and scholars began the process of filling in the missing accounts of their lives and communities in Canadian histories (Bannerji 1987; Bristow 1994; Burnet 1986)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "119162e6-2adc-4d7e-8a36-de38bd1a91d9",
                                                "sense_id": "65c65e4f-9a9f-3abe-a810-d08d06d41be5",
                                                "text": "Though still a numeric minority, more racialized women continue to make inroads into the academy as students, professors, and researchers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f7fa7a0-30c4-4ce6-9ec8-f10c7853c9a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a06292-1553-3a3d-a912-6a6db5d1e394",
                        "target_lang_word": "of color",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "of color",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dae596a1-20bb-3454-9868-1e86a3163718",
                                        "entry_id": "520be3c4-176b-3ab8-a439-f8d2476987a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nonwhite; of a race other than white, for example black."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4723b97-495c-4801-a2da-e336983220b3",
                                                "sense_id": "dae596a1-20bb-3454-9868-1e86a3163718",
                                                "text": "It is to him that we owe the story that Talleyrand outraged the susceptibilities of the Philadelphians by his open admiration for a woman of colour with whom he frequently appeared in public."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc792c86-c3d3-473e-ae0e-60c3f5f548d4",
                                                "sense_id": "dae596a1-20bb-3454-9868-1e86a3163718",
                                                "text": "But the vengeance I told myself I was getting for Wrex felt like a lie. I could win the game but he wasn't coming back. Being forced to lose my in-game comrade-who I thought of as a virtual person of color and as a brother-in-arms-affected me in a forceful way that I never expected. Mass Effect made me look at myself and think about the way races, classes and individuals bring their histories to bear."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2db1525-24ee-49aa-bc26-4b2e553aa16f",
                                                "sense_id": "dae596a1-20bb-3454-9868-1e86a3163718",
                                                "text": "She's also worked to help librarians forge connections through professional activities. Bell cochaired the first Joint Council of Librarians of Color (JCLC) in 2006, the first-ever shared conference among ALA's five ethnic affiliate associations: BCALA, the American Indian Library Association, the Asian/Pacific American Librarians Association, the Chinese American Librarians Association, and Reforma."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b4e5a7b-f50e-4b97-b752-9cb3536e64e1",
                                                "sense_id": "dae596a1-20bb-3454-9868-1e86a3163718",
                                                "text": "...historians and Native Americans are also revisiting the legacy of Charles Curtis, whose Kaw Nation ancestry gives him a claim as the first \"person of color\" to serve as vice president, although the term's current usage emerged decades later."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "763037c0-b6bd-34d5-98c1-f135f64fe8b5",
                                        "entry_id": "520be3c4-176b-3ab8-a439-f8d2476987a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belonging to a category of people with mixed black and white ancestry in the Americas in the 18th and early 19th centuries."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d962116-3364-47ca-bb74-830783ab3a93",
                                                "sense_id": "763037c0-b6bd-34d5-98c1-f135f64fe8b5",
                                                "text": "[page 1:] Chap. 1. … The inhabitants of the French part of St. Domingo, as of all the West Indian Islands, were composed of three great classes: 1st, Pure whites. 2d, People of colour, and blacks of free condition. 3d, Negroes in a state of slavery. The reader is apprised that the class which, by a strange abuse of language, is called people of colour, originates from an intermixture of the whites and the blacks. The genuine offspring of a pure white with a negro is called a mulatto; but there are various casts, …. All these were known in St. Domingo by the term sang-melées, or gens de couleur …\n[page 67:] Chap. VI. Consequences in St. Domingo of the Decree of the 15th of May—Rebellion of the Negroes in the Northern Province, and Enormities committed by them—Revolt of the Mulattoes at Mirebalais—Concordat or Truce between the Inhabitants of Port au Prince and the Men of Colour of the 13th of September—Proclamation by the National Assembly of the 20th of September."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e230ef7-5800-43f1-81d9-c3d450865914",
                                                "sense_id": "763037c0-b6bd-34d5-98c1-f135f64fe8b5",
                                                "text": "Those who owned the smaller plots were mainly poor whites, free people of color, and free blacks, none of whom had been affected by emancipation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b20a5d-bdfc-4f44-b921-37d5af93192d",
                                                "sense_id": "763037c0-b6bd-34d5-98c1-f135f64fe8b5",
                                                "text": "For quotations using this term, see Citations:of color."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "19188d70-7036-4e69-b0df-f3f37a6cadb1",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5a06292-1553-3a3d-a912-6a6db5d1e394",
                        "target_lang_word": "цветной",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "цветной",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35aacfa7-a365-34ec-87a2-66c5d10453e3",
                                        "entry_id": "e92d3816-b001-33ff-acbb-c87087dcc5a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "окрашенный в несколько разных цветов"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa2a6732-cb2f-41dc-9f2f-3fa2511201bd",
                                                "sense_id": "35aacfa7-a365-34ec-87a2-66c5d10453e3",
                                                "text": "На передних санях сидел Ларивон и какая-то баба в цветной шали."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09b54a27-e03b-4f59-afe5-c83a8a379c4f",
                                                "sense_id": "35aacfa7-a365-34ec-87a2-66c5d10453e3",
                                                "text": "Работа была несложная: набивать цветной узор на нарезанные куски ткани."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                        "entry_id": "e92d3816-b001-33ff-acbb-c87087dcc5a4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "способный распознавать или воспроизводить более чем один цвет"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "524991c0-879c-4023-85cc-b37fd8abc6e3",
                                                "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                                "text": "«А самое большое детское мученье: неочиненный или сломанный цветной карандаш»."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3a697ac-a6a7-4093-bb74-eb67d8012a01",
                                                "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                                "text": "Уже сейчас, благодаря замечательным достижениям науки, полностью разработаны и освоены разнообразные методы цветной киносъёмки; на фабриках налажено производство специальной плёнки для цветных кинофильмов."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d2999e9-0135-4c1e-81a4-252b4e4f0ed2",
                                                "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                                "text": "Фотографирование с таким осветителем под водой на цветные фотоплёнки, сенсобилизированные к солнечному свету, даёт вполне удовлетворительные результаты."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3bd886c-6c31-43c7-9c7a-60ad21f01f79",
                                                "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                                "text": "Раздвинулись шторы, и осветился огромный экран цветного телевизора."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31c3a775-925f-4313-83bf-d48d4522a7f4",
                                                "sense_id": "effa23ef-3264-38bc-90df-1c50fa5e3507",
                                                "text": "В январе 2004 года на российском рынке появились новые модели цветных принтеров Oki C9000 и C7000 — серии V2."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "цветной",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea388104-ea0f-3261-bd2e-7b8f196047c4",
                                        "entry_id": "9c88a642-9f1d-3502-9851-105bb99b7933",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "субстантивир. человек, имеющий смешанное расовое происхождение: как правило — европеоидно-негроидное"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2b03571-366e-4088-be1c-1742d9e395ae",
                                                "sense_id": "ea388104-ea0f-3261-bd2e-7b8f196047c4",
                                                "text": "В Берлин приехало много иностранцев, цветных, чёрных, и к ним относились подчёркнуто внимательно."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
